{
  "about": "Classes: adventuring callings a member of an ancestry can take, with Orsino's chassis. hitDie and attributes add to the rolled character (Orsino's classModifier overlay); abilities are known from creation (melee or ranged is added from the equipped weapon); weapons and armor are the starting tables; proficiencies bound what can be equipped; specializations are the trait choices (a mage school, a cleric domain, a warrior disposition), chosen at creation; spellcasting gives a caster's slots by spell level for each character level to 20 (an old-school table that reaches Orsino's spell levels; one more first-level slot for a casting attribute of 14 or more); slots is Orsino's single pool, kept for reference; a class without it casts no levelled spells. features are what a calling brings at later levels (techniques it learns and calling traits it takes), Kyr's own progression from executable Orsino techniques and modifiers.",
